        ":question/problem": "Rewrite the following expression as the sum of a perfect square and a constant.\n\n$({x}^{2}+12x+{6}^{2})+4=($\n{{field-1}}${)}^{2}+$\n{{field-2}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall the following formula:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2ax+{a}^{2}={(x+a)}^{2}\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a perfect square in the parentheses that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+12x+{6}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2} & = \\\\ {(x+6)}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+12x+{6}^{2})+4 & = \\\\ {(\\,x+6\\,)}^{2}+4 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"
